    lede:"Born in Pennsylvania on 17 February 1828, the son of Phillip Miller and Elizabeth Victor, whose surname became his given name. In 1860 he was 30 and living in Georges Township with his wife Jane and three small children, the eldest William, 5; by 1880 there were more than a dozen. Widowed, he died at Fairchance of pleurisy on 22 May 1911, aged 83, and was buried in the Miller Cemetery. William named a son Franklin Victor.",
